# The wait reaches green and stops there

The half-applied fix, and the case that makes segmentation load bearing.

Both branches edit two labels, so both need the gap. Here green has it and red
does not — the shape of an author who fixed the branch the issue quoted.

A guard that drops the `green` / `red` split and asks the file-wide question
"is there a wait somewhere between the first label command and the last" answers
yes and goes green, while red still fires two label events in the same second.
Nothing else in this directory dies when the split is removed: the ordering
cases reject with or without it.
